window.EXPLAIN=window.EXPLAIN||{};window.EXPLAIN.en={"1000":{"text":"A warning sign announces a place where traffic will be disrupted and you must expect to slow down or stop. So you reduce speed and increase the gap in advance."},"1001":{"text":"Sign A-16 warns of a marked pedestrian crossing you are approaching. From that sign on you owe particular caution and readiness to give way to a pedestrian."},"1003":{"text":"Sign A-17 warns of a place frequently used by children, near a school or a playground for instance. A child runs into the road without warning, so you slow down here even when nobody is in sight."},"10081":{"law":"art. 31 ust. 2 pkt 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A vehicle with faulty steering must not be towed at all, because it cannot be steered behind the towing car. Such a vehicle goes on a flatbed."},"1009":{"text":"Sign A-20 announces a stretch of road with two-way traffic, where oncoming vehicles will appear. It usually stands where a one-way carriageway ends or a diversion leads onto the other side."},"10109":{"law":"art. 31 ust. 2 pkt 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A motorcycle being towed must have both braking systems working, front and rear, because it brakes itself. Speed makes no difference here."},"1015":{"text":"A steep ascent is announced by sign A-23 and a steep descent by A-22, told apart by which way the triangle in the pictogram rises. Here the warning is about something else, so the answer is no."},"1018":{"text":"Sign A-24 warns of a place where cyclists enter or cross the road, usually before a cycle crossing. Particular caution applies there, and overtaking is prohibited on the crossing and immediately before it."},"1025":{"text":"Sign A-28 warns of a road covered with loose gravel, which flies from under the wheels into other vehicles' lights and windows. You slow down and lengthen the gap, because gravel also stretches the braking distance."},"1028":{"text":"Sign A-29 announces that traffic at the next junction is controlled by light signals. It is placed where the signal head comes into view late, for example beyond a bend or a crest."},"1033":{"law":"art. 19 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A shoulder can be soft, sunken or full of gravel, and the drop from the tarmac can pull the car off the road. You move onto it slowly and with no sharp steering."},"1035":{"text":"A sign with a plate giving the length of the section warns about that whole section at once. Individual bends will not be signed separately, so you stay extra cautious to the end of the stated distance."},"1052":{"text":"Red road studs mark the right-hand edge of the carriageway. White ones are used at the left edge and on the centre line, so that at night you know at once which side of the road you are on."},"1055":{"text":"Red studs mark the right edge of the carriageway, so beyond them the carriageway ends. What follows is the shoulder or the kerb, not another lane."},"1056":{"text":"White studs do not mark the right edge of the carriageway, so the shoulder does not begin directly beyond them. The right-hand edge is marked in red."},"1058":{"text":"White studs do not stand for the edge of the carriageway: white marks the centre line and the left edge, as well as the run of the lanes. The right edge is always marked in red."},"10805":{"law":"art. 5 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The signals of the escort of an oversize vehicle must be obeyed like a police officer's, because the escort directs traffic while the load passes. Their signals override the road signs."},"10806":{"law":"art. 39 ust. 3 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A rear-facing child seat in the front is allowed only with the passenger airbag switched off. A deploying airbag would strike the child straight in the head."},"10815":{"text":"A child seat is fitted exactly as the manufacturer describes, because only in that configuration did it pass crash testing. Comfort and looks have nothing to do with it."},"10816":{"law":"art. 135 ust. 1 pkt 1a Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The officer takes the licence when the limit is exceeded by more than 50 km/h in a built-up area. Exactly 50 km/h is not yet that case, and outside built-up areas the rule does not apply."},"10819":{"text":"The starosta issues the decision to withhold the licence for exceeding the limit by more than 50 km/h in a built-up area. Outside built-up areas this rule does not apply."},"10822":{"text":"The licence is withheld for 3 months. If the driver drives anyway, the period is extended to 6 months, and a further breach can mean the licence being revoked."},"10829":{"law":"art. 71 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Admission of a vehicle to traffic is evidenced by the registration certificate. The vehicle card records its history, and the windscreen control sticker has not been used since 2019."},"10840":{"law":"art. 39 ust. 3 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A child under 150 cm travels in a child seat or another restraint matched to their height and weight. A child must never be carried on a passenger's lap."},"10869":{"law":"art. 39 ust. 3 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A child under 150 cm must travel in a child seat or another restraint, in the front seat too. Carrying them with no restraint and no belt fastened is not allowed anywhere in the car."},"10871":{"text":"The child seat is installed according to the manufacturer's instructions, because only then do its anchorages and straps work. Nobody's comfort changes the fitting rules."},"10872":{"text":"A restraint is fitted the way the manufacturer recommends, because that is how it was tested and approved. Improvising the installation cancels out all the protection."},"10874":{"law":"art. 39 ust. 3 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A child under three may only travel in a car fitted with seat belts and in a child seat. Without belts the seat cannot be secured, so such a vehicle must not carry the child."},"10876":{"text":"A child seat is chosen by its technical requirements: approval, and the child's height and weight. Comfort and looks are secondary, because protection comes from meeting the standard."},"10878":{"law":"art. 39 ust. 3a Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A child at least 135 cm tall may travel on the rear seat on belts alone if their height and weight make a child seat unusable. The threshold is 135 cm, not 125 cm, and no speed limit applies here."},"10880":{"law":"art. 39 ust. 3a Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The condition is a height of at least 135 cm and that the child's height and weight rule out a restraint. A speed limit has nothing to do with it."},"10882":{"law":"art. 39 ust. 3 pkt 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"If two children are already in child seats and a third seat cannot be fitted, a third child over 3 may be secured with the belts alone. A child is never carried on an adult's lap."},"10883":{"law":"art. 39 ust. 3 pkt 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The third child, for whom there is no room for a restraint, is secured with the seat belts. A footrest or the middle seat changes nothing."},"10885":{"law":"art. 38 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"You must carry the receipt for a retained registration certificate for as long as it authorises driving. The certificate itself and proof of insurance payment need not be carried in Poland, the data is in the register."},"10886":{"law":"art. 38 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"You carry the receipt for a retained temporary permit for as long as it allows the vehicle to be used. Comprehensive insurance is voluntary, and the inspection certificate need not be carried."},"10887":{"law":"art. 38 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Since 2018 the registration certificate need not be carried, but the receipt for its retention must be, because it then stands in for the vehicle document. The officer checks the data in the central vehicle register."},"10888":{"law":"art. 38 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"What is compulsory is the receipt for a retained temporary permit during the period it authorises driving. Neither the EC certificate of conformity nor the registration certificate has to be carried."},"10889":{"law":"art. 38 pkt 3 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Driving a foreign-registered car you must carry the document admitting it to traffic, because that vehicle is not in the Polish registers. Accident insurance is voluntary, and a copy of the inspection certificate replaces nothing."},"10890":{"law":"art. 38 pkt 3 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"With a foreign-registered vehicle you carry the document confirming compulsory third-party cover. The Polish registers hold no insurance data for such a car."},"10891":{"law":"art. 38 pkt 3 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"With a foreign-registered car you must have proof that the third-party premium has been paid. Motorway tolls and proof of ownership are not documents required at a roadside check."},"10892":{"law":"art. 38 pkt 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A Polish licence need not be carried, since the entitlement is in the register, but a foreign document must be with you. A certificate of professional competence concerns professional drivers only."},"10893":{"law":"art. 38 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The receipt for a retained driving licence must be carried, because during that time it stands in for the entitlement document. Medical and psychological certificates concern professional drivers."},"10894":{"law":"art. 38 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The driver carries the receipt for the retained licence throughout the period it authorises driving. Psychological and medical certificates are not on that list for an ordinary driver."},"10895":{"law":"art. 38 pkt 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"What is compulsory is an entitlement document other than a Polish licence, for example a foreign or international one. Course certificates are not roadside check documents."},"10898":{"law":"art. 135 ust. 1 pkt 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The licence is taken for carrying more people than the seats entered in the registration certificate. Overtaking across a solid line or meeting a vehicle on a level crossing brings a fine and points, but not the loss of the document."},"10899":{"law":"art. 135 ust. 1 pkt 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The ground for taking the licence is carrying more people than the seats entered in the temporary permit. Overtaking before a crossing where traffic is directed is legal, and meeting a vehicle on a cycle crossing is an offence that does not cost the document."},"1091":{"text":"A prohibition sign takes effect from the point where it stands, not from the next junction or from a plate. If the ban is to start further on, a plate with the distance says so."},"1092":{"text":"A plate giving a length under a prohibition sign states over what stretch of road the ban applies. Once that distance is covered the ban ends without any cancelling sign."},"10930":{"text":"The receipt authorises driving for 24 hours from the moment the licence was taken. After that, driving counts as driving without a licence."},"10931":{"text":"Here too the receipt is good for 24 hours, whatever the licence was taken for. The clock starts at the moment the document is retained."},"10960":{"law":"art. 135 ust. 1a Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The licence is not taken if the speeding served to save life or health. The law expressly excludes acting out of necessity."},"10961":{"law":"art. 135 ust. 1a Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The officer will refrain from taking the licence, because the driver acted to save a human life. There is no caution with a re-test here, and no extra training either."},"10992":{"law":"art. 39 ust. 3 pkt 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The third child may be secured with belts alone only when two are already in child seats, a third seat cannot be fitted, and the child is over 3. A height of 100 cm or an age of 15 is not the condition here."},"10994":{"law":"art. 39 ust. 4 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The only exemption comes from a medical certificate stating a contraindication to a child seat. No room for a seat, or a height of 135 cm, does not lift the requirement in the front seat."},"11001":{"law":"art. 38 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A driver whose entitlement is limited to a car with an alcohol interlock must carry the inspection certificate covering that device. The registration certificate and proof of insurance need not be carried."},"11003":{"text":"A road transport inspector has the same powers as the police here and may check the vehicle in the central vehicle register. A transport check with no access to that data would be pointless."},"11005":{"law":"art. 132 ust. 5 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The registration certificate is returned by the vehicle testing station after an inspection matching the reason it was taken. Only confirmation that the fault is gone brings the document back."},"11017":{"text":"For exceeding the limit by more than 50 km/h in a built-up area the licence is withheld for 3 months. Driving despite the ban extends that to 6 months."},"11018":{"text":"The receipt allows driving for 24 hours from the moment the licence was taken. It is meant to let you get home, not to carry on driving as usual."},"11022":{"law":"art. 135 ust. 1a Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The exception is acting to avert an immediate danger to a legally protected interest, that is necessity. Pressure from another driver or wanting to clear a junction faster excuses nothing."},"11028":{"law":"art. 39 ust. 3 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"With the passenger airbag active a child may travel in front only in a forward-facing child seat. Any rear-facing arrangement requires the airbag to be switched off."},"1127":{"law":"art. 24 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"You may begin overtaking only with enough visibility and room to return to your lane without cutting anyone up. If either condition is missing, you abandon the manoeuvre."},"11528":{"law":"art. 135 ust. 1 pkt 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Exceeding the number of seats by two people or more costs a 3-month withholding of the licence. A check of driving qualifications is not part of this penalty."},"1181":{"law":"art. 24 ust. 5 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"You may pass on the right a vehicle that is signalling a left turn and has moved towards the centre of the road. You then use the free space on the right, having checked that nobody is coming through it."},"1202":{"text":"Warning signs do not announce snowfall, because weather is not signed with a fixed sign. They warn of the effects on the road, such as a slippery surface or frost."},"1203":{"text":"Sign A-33 warns of a place where traffic jams form often. Beyond it you must expect the queue to stop suddenly and keep a bigger gap."},"1292":{"text":"A signal forbidding entry applies unconditionally and cannot be worked around by claiming you obstruct nobody. Not obstructing others is no legal ground for passing the signal."},"13052":{"law":"art. 19 ust. 3 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A strictly defined minimum gap applies on motorways and expressways: at least half the number shown on the speedometer, expressed in metres. On other roads the gap simply has to be safe."},"13054":{"law":"art. 20 ust. 5 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A vehicle with a device sticking out more than 1.5 m ahead of the driver's seat may do at most 30 km/h in a built-up area and 60 km/h outside it. The protruding part hides the road right in front, hence the lower limit."},"13058":{"law":"art. 19 ust. 1 i art. 20 ust. 3 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"On a motorway a car may do at most 140 km/h, and only when conditions still let you keep control. The limit is an upper bound, not a recommended speed."},"13064":{"law":"art. 20 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"In a built-up area the limit is 50 km/h and it applies to a quadricycle too, whatever its weight. Weight changes the limits only outside built-up areas and for combinations with a trailer."},"13088":{"law":"art. 31 ust. 1 pkt 3 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Towing is allowed at up to 30 km/h in a built-up area and 60 km/h outside it. The towed car often has weaker brakes and no servo assistance, so going faster is simply dangerous."},"13382":{"law":"art. 39 ust. 4 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The only exemption is a medical certificate stating a contraindication to a child seat. Driving slower or a sticker announcing a child on board does not lift the requirement."},"13402":{"law":"art. 26 ust. 6 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A white cane marks a blind person, and then the driver must stop the vehicle and let them cross, including away from a marked crossing. A horn only disorients such a person."},"13404":{"law":"art. 26 ust. 1 i 6 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A person with a visible disability needs more time, so you have to assume in advance that you will have to stop. Approaching the crossing at a speed that makes stopping impossible is the mistake."},"13460":{"law":"art. 28 ust. 6 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"If the vehicle cannot be cleared off the track, you must warn the train driver, because a train takes hundreds of metres to stop. You warn from a suitable distance, with a clear signal visible from the cab."},"13461":{"law":"art. 28 ust. 5 i 6 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The first thing to do is get the vehicle off the crossing, and only if that fails do you warn the train driver. The order is such because a clear crossing solves the problem, while a warning only announces it."},"13463":{"text":"Barriers are built so that they can be broken through if a car is trapped between them. Better to wreck a barrier than to stay on the track in front of an approaching train."},"13464":{"law":"art. 28 ust. 3 pkt 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Once the half-barriers start coming down, entering the crossing is prohibited, however carefully you drive. Their lowering means a train is on its way and will be there in moments."},"13522":{"law":"art. 26 ust. 6 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"For a person with visibly limited mobility the duty to stop applies away from a marked crossing as well. Such a person cannot get out of the way or step back in front of an approaching car."},"13540":{"law":"art. 23 ust. 1 pkt 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"When passing a pedestrian you must keep a safe gap and, if needed, slow down. A pedestrian may step aside, so passing close at full speed is out of the question."},"13551":{"law":"art. 30 ust. 3 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"In fog outside a built-up area the driver of a motor vehicle gives short sound signals when overtaking, including when overtaking a pedestrian. A pedestrian will not hear a quiet car and will not step aside in time."},"13552":{"law":"art. 30 ust. 3 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The same duty covers passing a stationary pedestrian: in fog outside a built-up area you give short sound signals. The point is that the pedestrian hears the vehicle before it draws level."},"13553":{"law":"art. 26 ust. 6 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"At a stop with no island the passengers step straight onto the roadway, so the driver must stop in a place that leaves them free access to the vehicle. Driving past a standing bus without stopping is an offence."},"13560":{"law":"art. 19 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The duty to drive at a speed that keeps the vehicle under control applies to every driver, a cyclist and a cart driver included. It depends neither on the type of vehicle nor on the area."},"13561":{"law":"art. 19 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A safe speed is the one at which you keep control of the vehicle in the current conditions. It is often far below the legal limit, for instance on ice or in fog."},"13562":{"law":"art. 19 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"You drive slowly enough to stop before an obstacle within the stretch of road you can see, whatever the limit says. At night or in fog that means far below the legal maximum."},"13569":{"text":"The faster you go, the less time is left to notice a hazard and react. Reaction time is roughly constant, so at higher speed the car covers a longer distance during it."},"13570":{"text":"Impact energy grows with the square of speed, so speed decides the outcome of every crash, not only a head-on one. The gap between 50 and 70 km/h is the gap between a dented wing and a fatality."},"13580":{"law":"art. 19 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"At night on a winding unlit road the headlights reach less far than the stopping distance at the maximum limit. You have to drive so as to stop within the range of your own lights."},"13592":{"text":"A very fast vehicle is harder to spot, because others judge distance and closing time from typical speeds. That is why a driver joining the road pulls out right in front of a speeding car."},"13593":{"text":"At 120 km/h a car covers about 33 metres per second, so one second of delay adds over thirty metres to the stopping distance. That alone can be the difference between avoiding and hitting."},"13594":{"text":"100 km/h is about 28 metres per second, since you divide kilometres per hour by 3.6. The conversion is worth remembering: at 50 km/h a car covers roughly 14 metres a second."},"13604":{"law":"art. 33a ust. 3 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"An electric scooter is built for one person and carrying a passenger is prohibited. A second rider shifts the centre of gravity and lengthens the braking distance of a vehicle that brakes poorly anyway."},"13609":{"law":"art. 60 ust. 2 pkt 4 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Towing behind the vehicle a person on a mobility device, such as a scooter or skates, is prohibited. That person has no way to brake or to react to what the driver does."},"13615":{"law":"art. 33a ust. 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A footway may be used exceptionally, when there is no cycle path and the speed limit on the road exceeds 30 km/h. You then ride at walking pace and give way to pedestrians."},"13618":{"law":"art. 28 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Raised barriers do not remove the duty to make sure no train is coming. Safety devices do fail, and responsibility for entering the crossing always rests with the driver."},"13623":{"law":"art. 28 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Approaching a crossing you watch the signals, the barriers, the audible warnings and the track itself in both directions. A train cannot brake in time, so the whole check falls on the driver."},"1366":{"text":"Sign B-1 prohibits all vehicles in both directions on the road it stands by. Placed at one carriageway of a dual road it applies to that carriageway, but there it blocks traffic both ways."},"1368":{"text":"A no-entry ban applies whatever your reason for going in. The purpose of the trip, including reaching a business by the road, does not lift the ban unless a plate under the sign does."},"13684":{"text":"Prudence means raising your attention where the risk is real, that is at a pedestrian crossing. Constantly driving at the limit ignores changing conditions, and maximum acceleration reduces no danger."},"1369":{"text":"Sign B-22 prohibits turning right beyond it and applies at the nearest junction. The ban holds regardless of whether the turn would obstruct anyone."},"13769":{"law":"art. 24 ust. 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The minimum of 1 metre applies to overtaking, not to meeting an oncoming vehicle. Passing something coming the other way requires simply a safe gap."},"13834":{"law":"art. 24 ust. 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"An electric scooter falls under the same rule as a bicycle: at least 1 metre of clearance when overtaking. A scooter easily loses balance on a bump, so passing close can knock it over."},"13835":{"law":"art. 20 ust. 6 pkt 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"An electric scooter may do at most 20 km/h, whatever it is capable of. On a footway it is additionally limited to something close to walking pace."},"13850":{"law":"art. 19 ust. 1 i art. 28 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Heavy rain or snow cuts visibility exactly where you need to spot an approaching train. So before a crossing you slow down more than usual, to have time to look and to stop."},"13859":{"law":"art. 24 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Before every overtake you must make sure there is enough visibility and room, and that the manoeuvre will obstruct nobody. That is an absolute condition, whatever the road and the time of day."},"13862":{"law":"art. 24 ust. 7 pkt 3 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Inside a built-up area overtaking a privileged vehicle is prohibited. It may change course or accelerate hard at any moment, and passers-by are watching it, not you."},"13863":{"law":"art. 24 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Overtaking always demands particular caution, because you move into a lane you were not using and lose part of your view. It is the manoeuvre that causes the most crashes."},"13866":{"law":"art. 24 ust. 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A column of pedestrians falls under the same rule as a single pedestrian: at least 1 metre when overtaking. A column takes more room and its edge can shift at any moment."},"13880":{"law":"art. 33a ust. 3 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Towing one electric scooter with another is prohibited. Both become uncontrollable, and braking on one throws the other off line."},"13882":{"law":"art. 135 ust. 1 pkt 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"For an offence that created a serious danger to safety a court may impose a driving ban, and the officer may retain the licence. What counts is the consequence, not only the fact of exceeding the limit."},"13883":{"law":"art. 19 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Safe speed follows from the conditions, not from the sign: on an icy road 30 km/h may be safe where 90 is allowed. Staying within the limit does not by itself make a speed safe."},"13884":{"text":"Yes, that is the standard penalty: exceeding the limit by more than 50 km/h in a built-up area costs 3 months without the licence. A heavy fine and penalty points come on top."},"13885":{"law":"art. 19 ust. 2 pkt 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Driving unreasonably slowly is prohibited, because it holds up traffic and provokes risky overtaking. On a fast road a crawling car can be as dangerous as a speeding one."},"13886":{"text":"A disabled parking card gives parking privileges and allows certain prohibition signs to be disregarded, but it does not raise the speed limit. No document changes the speed rules."},"13891":{"law":"art. 39 ust. 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Among those exempt from wearing a belt is a disabled person carried in a wheelchair. Feeling uncomfortable in a belt is no exemption at all."},"13893":{"law":"art. 66 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A vehicle is admitted to traffic if it is kept in a state that endangers neither its occupants nor other road users. Air conditioning and tinted windows have nothing to do with admission."},"13902":{"law":"art. 19 ust. 3 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"On a motorway the gap is at least half the speedometer reading in metres, so at 140 km/h that is 70 metres, not 60. The rule is simple: halve your speed."},"13903":{"law":"art. 19 ust. 3 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"On a dual-carriageway expressway the limit is 120 km/h, so the gap is at least 60 metres, not 50. It is always half the number on the speedometer."},"13904":{"law":"art. 19 ust. 3 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The half-the-speed rule applies on motorways and dual-carriageway expressways, and it does not apply while overtaking. If it did, the manoeuvre could never be completed."},"13909":{"text":"A worn tread clears far less water than a new one, so the tyre loses contact with the tarmac sooner. With little tread left, aquaplaning starts at a speed where a new tyre still grips."},"13910":{"text":"In heavy rain a film of water builds between tyre and tarmac and the car stops responding to steering and brakes. That is aquaplaning, and it ends in loss of control."},"13911":{"law":"art. 19 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The limit is an upper bound, not a guarantee of safety: in fog or on black ice even a speed within the rules can be too high. The duty to keep control applies regardless of the signs."},"13912":{"law":"art. 19 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The law expressly lists traffic intensity, alongside terrain, the state and visibility of the road, the state of the vehicle and the weather. A weather forecast and one's own experience are not in that list."},"13915":{"text":"At high speed the eyes fix far ahead and the field of vision narrows sharply. That is why a driver on a fast road stops registering the verge and the side entrances."},"13916":{"law":"art. 26 ust. 6 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"For a person with visibly limited mobility the duty to stop is unconditional and applies away from a crossing as well. There is no room here to judge whether they will make it across."},"13917":{"text":"A disabled bay is wider precisely so that a door can be opened and a wheelchair rolled out. Taking even part of it destroys the whole point of the bay."},"13918":{"text":"Centrifugal force grows with the square of speed, so in a bend every increase pushes the car outwards. Once it exceeds tyre grip, the vehicle leaves its line."},"13919":{"text":"Doubling the speed in a bend quadruples the centrifugal force, because it depends on the square of speed. That is why a small dab of throttle mid-corner makes a far bigger difference than it seems."},"13920":{"text":"The wheels of a lorry throw out a wall of water that blanks the windscreen for a moment. So before meeting one you slow down and set the wipers to their fastest speed."},"13921":{"text":"The arms on the wheel should be slightly bent at the elbows: only then can you turn the wheel fully without lifting your back off the seat. Straight arms cost precision, sharply bent ones cost strength."},"13923":{"text":"A head restraint level with the back of the head limits the whip of the head in a rear-end impact and protects the neck. One dropped to the level of the nape becomes a lever instead."},"13924":{"text":"A badly chosen position hampers control: a seat too far back stops you pressing the clutch fully, one too close blocks arm movement. The setting is individual, not just a matter of the extremes."},"13925":{"text":"The seat setting decides whether you reach the pedals and can turn the wheel fully, and also how the belt and airbag will work. It is a safety item, not a matter of comfort."},"13926":{"law":"art. 19 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Speed alone is not enough: the radius of the bend, the surface and its camber, the load and the view round the corner all count. You take a bend by what you can see, not by the speedometer."},"13927":{"text":"Taking a bend safely starts before it: you slow on the straight, choose your line and only then turn in. The line is chosen so as to see the exit of the bend for as long as possible."},"13928":{"text":"One hand on the wheel does not improve precision, it removes it: you can neither unwind the wheel quickly nor react to a snatch. The wheel is held with both hands, at the nine and three o'clock positions."},"13929":{"text":"A hand put through the wheel is struck by the deploying airbag and loses contact with the rim when the wheel snatches. This applies to every situation, not only parking."},"13932":{"law":"art. 135 ust. 1 pkt 1a Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Yes, for exceeding the limit by more than 50 km/h in a built-up area the officer takes the licence on the spot, against a receipt. The receipt allows another 24 hours of driving."},"13936":{"law":"art. 19 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The limit only says how fast you may go at most, not how fast is safe right now. In fog, on wet tarmac or in dense traffic the speed that keeps the car under control is much lower."},"13941":{"law":"art. 4 i art. 45 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Seeing dangerous behaviour on the road you warn others, for example with the hazard lights, and remove the danger where you can. Limited trust works both ways: you anticipate and you warn."},"13942":{"law":"art. 2 pkt 47b Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"By definition an electric scooter has no seat, it is ridden standing. A machine with a seat is a different category, a moped for instance, and falls under different rules."},"13943":{"law":"art. 4 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A warning gives others time to react and can prevent further incidents, for example a car running onto spilt oil. It does not, however, remove liability or guarantee that nothing will happen."},"13944":{"law":"art. 3a ust. 2 ustawy o kierujących pojazdami","text":"Outside a residential zone an electric scooter may be ridden from the age of 10 by someone holding a cycling card. From 18 no document is needed, and inside a residential zone no age applies."},"13945":{"text":"Insurers take the offence history into account, so speeding tickets push up the third-party premium at renewal. Losing a no-claims discount often costs more than the fine itself."},"13950":{"text":"A disability does not mean someone will break the rules, and no such assumption is made. What you must allow for is that the person may need more time and cannot get out of the way quickly."},"13951":{"law":"art. 24 ust. 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Overtaking an electric scooter requires at least 1 metre, not 0.5. The same distance covers bicycles, mopeds, motorcycles and pedestrians."},"13962":{"law":"art. 24 ust. 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A mobility device such as skates or a skateboard falls under the same rule: at least 1 metre when overtaking. Someone on such a device is even less stable than a cyclist."},"13975":{"law":"art. 26 ust. 3 pkt 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"On an unregulated pedestrian crossing and immediately before it overtaking is prohibited. The overtaking car blocks the view: it cannot see the pedestrian and the pedestrian cannot see it."},"13976":{"law":"art. 26 ust. 3 pkt 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The ban covers unregulated crossings, so where traffic is directed by lights or an officer overtaking is permitted. The signals separate pedestrians and vehicles in time."},"13985":{"law":"art. 26 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A person pushing a mobility device counts as a pedestrian, so stepping onto the crossing they have priority. Wheeling a bike or a scooter alongside does not change that pedestrian status."},"13986":{"law":"art. 26 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Towards a pedestrian on the crossing you owe particular caution and priority. A person pushing a mobility device is treated exactly like any other pedestrian."},"13987":{"law":"art. 51 ust. 3 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Main beam must not be used if it can dazzle anyone, pedestrians walking in a column included. A dazzled column loses its bearings and may drift onto the roadway."},"13991":{"law":"art. 26 ust. 6 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The special sign, a white cane or an armband with three dots, marks a blind person. Towards them the duty to stop applies everywhere, away from a crossing as well."},"13992":{"law":"art. 26 ust. 6 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A person with visibly limited mobility has the right to cross, and the driver has the duty to stop. The rule requires neither a marked crossing nor any document."},"13993":{"text":"A suggested crossing is not a pedestrian crossing in the legal sense, so there is no priority there. That does not excuse a lack of caution, because a pedestrian may step out there anyway."},"13994":{"law":"art. 4 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A suggested crossing looks like a place to cross, so a pedestrian often steps out there without hesitating. Limited trust tells you to assume exactly that and slow down in advance."},"13995":{"law":"art. 23 ust. 1 pkt 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"When meeting a pedestrian you must, if needed, move to the right, slow down and even stop. On a narrow road the pedestrian has nowhere to go, so it is the driver who gives way."},"14002":{"law":"art. 26 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A person pushing a mobility device is a pedestrian, and a pedestrian stepping onto the crossing has priority. The driver must give way, not judge whether they can slip through first."},"14007":{"law":"art. 4 i art. 45 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Spilt oil is a lethal trap, especially for motorcyclists, so you warn others and call the services. Driving off and saying nothing means abandoning a hazard you created yourself."},"14015":{"law":"art. 19 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Fatigue, illness or stress lengthen reaction time, so the safe speed for the same driver changes from day to day. After a night shift the safe speed is lower than after a good rest."},"14062":{"law":"art. 102 ust. 1d ustawy o kierujących pojazdami","text":"Driving despite the withholding extended to six months ends with the entitlement being revoked for 5 years. After that the licence has to be earned again, with all the exams."},"14063":{"law":"art. 102 ust. 1d ustawy o kierujących pojazdami","text":"The consequence is the same whatever the licence was taken for: the entitlement is revoked for 5 years. What counts is that the driver drove despite a ban in force."},"14064":{"law":"art. 135 ust. 1 pkt 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The licence is taken when the number of people carried exceeds the seats by more than two, that is by three or more. One or two extra means a fine and points, but not the loss of the document."},"14107":{"law":"art. 33b ust. 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"You must not ride a personal transport device along a pedestrian crossing; you cross it on foot, wheeling the device. The crossing is meant for walking across, not for riding along."},"1421":{"text":"The sign says that the crossing road you are approaching is a priority road. You must therefore give way to vehicles on it, whichever side they come from."},"1423":{"text":"A give-way sign does not order a stop: you stop only if there is no other way to yield. An unconditional stop at the line is ordered only by the B-20 stop sign."},"1427":{"text":"Sign B-21 prohibits turning left at the nearest junction and, along with it, turning around. The ban applies regardless of the traffic situation."},"1428":{"text":"Turning around is prohibited here by a sign: B-23 bans U-turns alone, while B-21 bans the left turn and with it the U-turn. The ban applies at the junction before which the sign stands."},"1430":{"text":"A prohibition sign placed within a junction refers only to the carriageway it stands by. On a dual road the signs therefore have to be read separately for each carriageway."},"1431":{"text":"A no-stopping ban covers the whole width of the road on that side, the shoulder included. Pulling off the carriageway does not lift the ban, because the shoulder is part of the road."},"1433":{"law":"art. 22 ust. 6 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"You may stop on the central reservation and wait for a gap, provided a U-turn is not prohibited there. The reservation gives you the room, and the car then blocks no traffic lane."},"1439":{"law":"art. 22 ust. 2 pkt 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"For a left turn you move in advance into the left lane or as close as possible to the centre of the road. Turning left from the right lane cuts across those driving alongside and is simply wrong."},"1448":{"law":"art. 22 ust. 2 pkt 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"For a right turn you move into the right lane in good time, not just before the junction. A last-second lane change surprises those alongside and forces them to brake."},"1451":{"text":"You choose the lane by the direction shown on the sign or by the arrows on the road, not by guesswork. Since your destination is served by the lane you are in, moving left is unnecessary."},"1452":{"text":"In a tunnel you use the lane designated for your direction, even when nobody else is around. An empty road does not lift the duty to stay in the correct lane."},"1459":{"law":"art. 49 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Around a marked stop without a bay, stopping is prohibited within 15 metres before and 15 metres after the sign. Eleven metres falls inside that range, so you may not stop there."},"1460":{"law":"art. 49 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The central reservation is not a place to stop: it is not meant for parked vehicles and a car standing there blocks the view. Stopping is allowed only while waiting to turn around, where that is permitted."},"1461":{"text":"A lay-by may be reserved for a specific use, for buses, taxis or service vehicles, and then parking there is prohibited. The sign or plate by the bay decides what it is for."},"1462":{"law":"art. 49 ust. 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A no-parking ban also covers the shoulder along that carriageway, because the shoulder is part of the road. Pulling onto it does not dodge the ban, any more than stopping half off the carriageway does."},"1464":{"law":"art. 49 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A no-stopping ban applies regardless of whether you obstruct anyone, and it covers the shoulder too. Not getting in the way is no exception to any ban expressed by a sign."},"1466":{"law":"art. 22 ust. 4 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"When changing lanes you give way to the vehicles already in that lane. Priority belongs to whoever is travelling there, and the one moving across has to fit in."},"1471":{"text":"The directions available from a lane are set by the arrows on the road or the sign above it, and they must be obeyed. From a lane that does not lead left you may not turn left."},"1473":{"text":"You may turn around only from a lane where a left turn is allowed. Since your lane leads elsewhere, a U-turn from it is prohibited."},"1474":{"text":"A U-turn is a left-hand manoeuvre, so it is made only from a lane where a left turn is allowed. From the other lanes it is prohibited, even on an empty road."},"1480":{"law":"art. 24 ust. 5 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"On a carriageway with at least two lanes in one direction, passing vehicles in the neighbouring lane is not overtaking in the legal sense. You stay in your own lane, so moving past a slower queue on the right is allowed."},"1482":{"law":"art. 24 ust. 7 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Overtaking is prohibited where visibility or room is lacking, and in places named by the rules: before a pedestrian crossing, on and before a level crossing, at a junction and where a sign forbids it. One of those grounds is enough."},"1484":{"law":"art. 24 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Overtaking without certainty about visibility and a clear road ends in a head-on crash, because the closing speed is the sum of both speeds. With two cars at 90 km/h you close a 50-metre gap every second."},"1490":{"law":"art. 22 ust. 6 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The signing of this road rules out a U-turn: either a sign forbids it or the nature of the road does, a one-way street, a motorway or an expressway. In each case the manoeuvre is prohibited whatever the conditions."},"1491":{"law":"art. 22 ust. 6 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A U-turn is prohibited in a tunnel, on a bridge or viaduct, on a one-way road, on a motorway and an expressway, and anywhere it would endanger safety. One of those grounds applies on this stretch."},"1492":{"law":"art. 22 ust. 6 pkt 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"On a bridge a U-turn is prohibited by the rules outright. A bridge is narrow, there is no shoulder and no room for the manoeuvre, and a car across it blocks both directions."},"1496":{"text":"A right turn is ruled out here by the signing: the lane arrows or a prohibition sign set the permitted directions. Changing lanes does not dodge the ban, because it applies to the whole carriageway at this point."},"1497":{"law":"art. 22 ust. 4 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Moving into the adjacent lane you give way to those already in it. The indicator announces your intention, it does not grant you priority."},"1498":{"law":"art. 22 ust. 5 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Every lane change is signalled with the indicator, moving into the right-hand lane included. You switch it on in good time and off as soon as the manoeuvre is complete."},"1500":{"law":"art. 22 ust. 5 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The duty to signal a lane change does not depend on where on the carriageway you are. The indicator informs not only those behind, but also those beside and ahead of you, and pedestrians."},"1503":{"law":"art. 22 ust. 5 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The intention to change lanes is always signalled with the indicator, and before you start moving across. An unsignalled manoeuvre surprises others and the consequences are on you."},"1504":{"law":"art. 22 ust. 4 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The driver moving into the adjacent lane never has priority, because it is they who change their course. They must find a gap and match their speed, not count on being let in."},"1505":{"text":"For a right turn you had to move into the right-hand lane in good time, and at this point it is too late. Crossing the lines and cutting across the carriageway right before the junction is prohibited."},"1510":{"text":"A lane change is ruled out here by the road marking: a solid line between the lanes may not be crossed. Solid lines are used exactly where the manoeuvre would be dangerous."},"1512":{"law":"art. 22 ust. 5 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The indicator is always compulsory, because it informs more than the drivers behind you. Your signal is also read by pedestrians, cyclists and drivers on the side road planning their own move."},"1514":{"law":"art. 22 ust. 6 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"At a junction a U-turn is allowed, provided no sign forbids it and the road is not one-way. You make it from a lane where a left turn is permitted, giving way to oncoming traffic."},"1516":{"text":"You may not turn into the nearest carriageway, because the signing forbids it: a no-turn sign or a one-way sign facing you. Entering against the flow is one of the most dangerous mistakes in town."},"1517":{"text":"Sign B-23 prohibits U-turns from where it stands up to and including the nearest junction. There is no cancelling sign to look for, the ban simply ends past that junction."},"1518":{"text":"Nothing here forbids a left turn: there is no prohibition sign and your lane permits that direction. When turning you give way to oncoming vehicles and to pedestrians on the crossing."},"1520":{"law":"art. 24 ust. 1 i 7 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Starting an overtake is out of the question here: either there is not enough visibility for the whole manoeuvre, or a ban applies from a sign, the road marking or the proximity of a junction. Any doubt is always settled by not going."},"1526":{"text":"A goods vehicle with a permissible maximum mass up to 3.5 tonnes follows the same overtaking rules as a car. Bans aimed at lorries normally apply to vehicles over 3.5 tonnes."},"1531":{"text":"The sign giving priority at a narrowing lets you enter, provided you do not force an oncoming driver to stop. It is the mirror image of sign B-31, where it is you who yields."},"1533":{"text":"A plate under the sign giving a distance shows how many metres separate the sign from the place it refers to. With a stop sign that means the distance to the point where you must stop."},"1540":{"text":"A prohibition sign applies as far as the nearest junction, unless a cancelling sign or the end of a zone lifts it earlier. That is the general rule for prohibition signs in Poland."},"1541":{"law":"art. 49 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A no-stopping ban covers any halting of the vehicle, even for a few seconds. A brief pause, dropping off a passenger or switching on the hazards changes nothing."},"1542":{"text":"A mandatory sign shows the only direction allowed beyond it. Since the arrow points left, at this junction you may go left and nowhere else."},"1578":{"law":"art. 49 ust. 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A no-parking ban applies however briefly you intend to stand. Five minutes is parking rather than stopping, so it falls squarely under the ban."},"1585":{"law":"art. 49 ust. 1 pkt 5 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"On a bridge, a viaduct and in a tunnel stopping is prohibited, and the purpose makes no difference. The structure is narrow, there is no shoulder and a standing car cannot be passed safely."},"1590":{"law":"art. 49 ust. 1 pkt 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Stopping is prohibited on a pedestrian crossing and within 10 metres before it, and on a two-way road with two lanes directly after it as well. A standing car hides a pedestrian stepping onto the crossing."},"1591":{"text":"A ban expressed by a sign is unconditional and cannot be satisfied by leaving room for others. The condition of not obstructing traffic applies to parking where there is no ban."},"1592":{"law":"art. 47 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Parking on a pavement is allowed only where a sign permits it, and on the terms that sign sets. Without such a sign a car on the pavement stands illegally, even if room is left for pedestrians."},"1600":{"law":"art. 16 ust. 4 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The rule is to drive as close to the right edge as practicable, with the left lane kept for overtaking. A sign does not order you into the left lane unless it assigns your direction to that lane only."},"1603":{"law":"art. 16 ust. 4 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"When several lanes lead straight on, you take the rightmost one that is practicable. Occupying the left lane without need blocks overtaking and is an offence."},"1647":{"law":"art. 4 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Limited trust tells you to assume that a cyclist may ride out or a pedestrian step out from behind anything blocking your view. A tram hides the whole lane beside it, so drive slowly enough to stop in time."},"1651":{"law":"art. 24 ust. 1 i 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A cyclist is overtaken with at least 1 metre of clearance and only when there is room and visibility for it. Since those conditions are missing, you do not attempt the manoeuvre."},"1864":{"law":"art. 6 ust. 1 pkt 3 ustawy o kierujących pojazdami","text":"A quadricycle other than a light one (up to 400 kg, engine over 15 kW) requires category B1. Category AM covers light quadricycles only, and category A is for motorcycles."},"1866":{"law":"art. 81 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The owner is obliged to have the vehicle inspected periodically. Personal accident and comprehensive insurance are voluntary; only third-party liability cover is compulsory."},"1876":{"text":"Check the pressure on cold tyres, right before setting off. After a drive the tyres are warm and the reading is too high, and a day in advance the pressure can still change."},"1877":{"law":"art. 61 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The load must not affect the stability of the vehicle. It must not cover the lights or number plates either, and it always has to be secured against shifting."},"1878":{"law":"art. 61 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The load is always secured against shifting. Driving slowly changes nothing, because a single braking manoeuvre or turn is enough to move it."},"1879":{"law":"art. 61 ust. 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A loose bulk load is carried in a sealed body, covered so that nothing spills onto the road. Low speed alone or the side boards do not achieve that."},"1880":{"law":"art. 61 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The fastening device must be secured so that it cannot work loose while driving. A dangling strap can be caught by a wheel or snag another vehicle."},"1881":{"law":"art. 61 ust. 3 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The load must not restrict the driver's view of the road. It must not cover the lights, reflectors or number plates either, not even slightly."},"1882":{"text":"The heaviest items go as low, as deep and as central as possible. Weight placed high or at the back raises the centre of gravity and worsens stability in bends and under braking."},"1883":{"law":"art. 61 ust. 3 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A load on a trailer must not cover its lights. It is also spread evenly, because a load pushed to one side or to the rear ruins the stability of the combination."},"1888":{"law":"art. 60 ust. 2 pkt 4 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Towing a person on skis, a sledge or roller skates behind the vehicle is prohibited. A CB radio is allowed, and a child in a seat may travel in front once the airbag is switched off."},"1905":{"text":"The extinguisher must be fixed in place and within the driver's reach, for example under a seat. A loose extinguisher becomes a projectile under braking, and one on the parcel shelf cannot be grabbed quickly."},"2025":{"text":"ASR is the traction control system: it stops the driven wheels from spinning when moving off and accelerating. Wheel lock-up under braking is handled by ABS."},"2026":{"text":"ESP stabilises the vehicle when it starts to slide or skid in a bend. Wheel lock-up is the job of ABS, and wheel spin when moving off is the job of ASR."},"2161":{"text":"With no sterile dressing at hand, use the casualty's own clean clothing and press on the wound. With a haemorrhage, delay is more dangerous than a non-sterile material."},"2164":{"text":"A pressure dressing is applied to a haemorrhage, to stop the blood flow. It is not used on a crushed limb or on discharge from the ear."},"2535":{"text":"In rain the first thing to do is slow down: braking distance grows and aquaplaning becomes likely. Turning traction control off or driving in the ruts only makes it worse."},"2536":{"text":"Once in a water-filled rut, reduce speed smoothly, with no abrupt inputs. Hard braking or acceleration during aquaplaning ends in loss of control."},"2538":{"text":"On a snowy road winter tyres are what helps, because they grip at low temperatures. The handbrake locks the rear axle and hard acceleration just spins the wheels."},"3187":{"text":"No amount of drugs improves risk assessment. They lengthen reaction time, distort judgement of distance and speed, and create a false sense of confidence."},"3232":{"text":"Alcohol narrows the field of attention, so divided attention suffers and doing two things at once gets harder. That is why a drinking driver misses a pedestrian while watching the lights."},"3340":{"text":"Moving off smoothly means releasing the clutch gradually while adding a little throttle. Dropping the pedal stalls the engine or jerks the car."},"3353":{"law":"art. 45 ust. 2 pkt 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Using a phone is prohibited if it requires holding the handset or microphone. A hands-free kit is allowed, and so is cruise control in a built-up area."},"3429":{"text":"In fog at night the first step is to slow down. Main beam reflects off the water droplets and dazzles you, and sitting right behind the car ahead leaves no room to brake."},"352":{"law":"art. 22 ust. 6 pkt 4 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The D-3 sign marks a one-way road, and on such a road turning around is prohibited. After a U-turn you would be driving against the flow, straight at vehicles with no room to avoid you."},"3523":{"text":"Drive through a large puddle after smoothly reducing speed. Braking or accelerating hard on water lifts the tyres off the surface."},"3573":{"law":"art. 44 ust. 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A witness to an accident must stop, call medical help and give first aid. That duty does not depend on who caused the accident."},"3625":{"law":"art. 23 ust. 1 pkt 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"When passing an oncoming vehicle the law requires a safe gap, not a fixed number of metres. What is safe depends on road width, speed and traffic conditions."},"3626":{"law":"art. 24 ust. 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The only gap given in metres applies to overtaking a bicycle, moped, motorcycle or pedestrian: at least 1 metre. Other manoeuvres just require a safe gap."},"3627":{"law":"art. 23 ust. 1 pkt 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"When passing a stationary obstacle the required gap is a safe one, depending on road width and traffic conditions. The law gives no fixed number of metres here."},"3628":{"law":"art. 24 ust. 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Overtaking a car requires a safe gap, depending on road width and traffic conditions. The fixed 1 metre applies only to bicycles, mopeds, motorcycles and pedestrians."},"3629":{"law":"art. 24 ust. 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"When overtaking a motorcycle you must leave a gap of at least 1 metre. The same rule covers bicycles, mopeds and pedestrians."},"3630":{"law":"art. 24 ust. 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A column of pedestrians is overtaken leaving at least 1 metre, exactly as a single pedestrian or a cyclist."},"3634":{"text":"Braking distance grows with the square of speed, so twice the speed means four times the distance. From 50 to 100 km/h the braking distance grows fourfold, not twofold."},"3650":{"law":"art. 19 ust. 3a Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Outside a built-up area, in a tunnel longer than 500 metres, a car keeps a gap of at least 50 metres. Vehicles over 3.5 tonnes keep 80 metres."},"3651":{"text":"Stopping distance is reaction distance plus braking distance, so the driver's reaction time feeds into it directly. In a passenger car the weight of the occupants is negligible here."},"3652":{"text":"Stopping distance depends directly on speed and road surface, because they decide the available grip and the energy to be shed. Passenger weight is negligible."},"3658":{"law":"art. 44 ust. 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The duty to help does not depend on medical qualifications. You do what you can: secure the scene, call for help and carry out basic life support."},"3723":{"text":"Compulsory equipment for a car in Poland is a warning triangle and a fire extinguisher. A first aid kit and a spare wheel are recommended but not required by law."},"3724":{"text":"A fire extinguisher is compulsory equipment in a car, together with the warning triangle. A first aid kit and a spare wheel are not."},"3759":{"law":"art. 30 ust. 1 i 3 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"In fog you may use front fog lights, instead of or together with dipped beam. Main beam bounces off the fog and dazzles you, and daytime running lights alone are not enough."},"3761":{"law":"art. 30 ust. 3 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"In fog outside a built-up area, a driver overtaking must give short sound signals. Rear fog lights are switched on only when visibility drops below 50 metres."},"3778":{"text":"When meeting a car at night, look to the right of its headlights and watch the verge there. Looking straight into the lights blinds you for seconds, and switching to main beam blinds the other driver."},"3781":{"text":"A xenon bulb must not be fitted into a reflector designed for a halogen bulb. The reflector then scatters the light outside its approval and dazzles other drivers, even if the base fits."},"3783":{"law":"art. 45 ust. 2 pkt 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Using a navigation device while driving is allowed. Unfastening the seat belt and using a phone that has to be held in the hand are prohibited."},"3784":{"text":"The minimum tread depth is 1.6 millimetres. Below that the tyre stops clearing water and the risk of aquaplaning rises sharply."},"3785":{"text":"A burnt-out indicator bulb is a lighting fault: other drivers cannot see what you intend to do. A dirty air filter or overheating plugs hurt performance but do not endanger traffic."},"3856":{"text":"Too little pressure on the pedal wastes the available grip and lengthens the braking distance. Locked wheels and loss of steering come from pressing too hard in a car without ABS."},"3857":{"text":"Without ABS, braking too hard locks the wheels, and locked wheels cannot steer the car. The steering stops working and the vehicle slides straight on."},"3858":{"text":"In a car with ABS you brake fast and hard, and the system keeps the wheels from locking. Pumping the pedal only gets in the ABS's way, repeating badly what it does better."},"3859":{"text":"The pulsing pedal means the ABS is working, so hold the pressure until the car stops. Easing off lengthens the braking distance, and releasing the pedal ends the braking altogether."},"3860":{"text":"ABS keeps the wheels from locking, so the car can still be steered even when you brake during a side skid. It works all the time, not only on a straight or only in a bend."},"3861":{"text":"On a hill, if you release the handbrake before the clutch starts to transmit drive, the car rolls back. Release it only when you feel the car pulling forward."},"3882":{"text":"A red brake warning lamp means a brake fault, so stop and check the fluid level. Driving on can end with no braking at all."},"3885":{"text":"The red coolant lamp warns that the coolant is too hot. Stop and let the engine cool, because overheating ends in serious damage."},"3889":{"text":"Fluid stains on the parking spot point to a leak, for example in the brake or cooling system. Colourless exhaust is normal, and so is the charging lamp before the engine is started."},"3890":{"text":"Thick black or blue exhaust smoke means the engine is burning too much fuel or oil. Colourless exhaust is normal, and the oil pressure lamp is always on before the engine starts."},"3891":{"text":"A space-saver spare may be used briefly and at reduced speed, that is exactly what it is for. Worn pads or discs and damaged shock absorbers take the car off the road."},"4160":{"law":"art. 30 ust. 1 pkt 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"With visibility under 50 metres you may switch on the rear fog lights so that drivers behind spot the car sooner. Main beam bounces off the fog, and closing the gap is plainly dangerous."},"4362":{"text":"The road is most slippery at the start of the rain, when water mixes with the dust and oil on the surface. After a longer shower that film is washed away and grip partly returns."},"4364":{"text":"The faster you drive, the narrower your field of vision becomes: the eyes focus on a point far ahead. That is why at speed it is easy to miss a pedestrian or a vehicle at the side."},"4367":{"text":"The field of vision is cut down by dazzle from oncoming headlights: the eye needs several seconds to recover. The interior mirror and the air conditioning do not take vision away."},"4368":{"text":"Badly aimed headlights light too short a stretch of road or point off to the side, so at night you simply do not see what is ahead. Aim is checked at the periodic inspection."},"4369":{"text":"Alcohol narrows the field of vision into tunnel vision, so the driver stops noticing what is at the sides. Blinking and a rest break work the other way round, they improve attention."},"4370":{"text":"A seat set too low or too high takes away part of the view: the pillars and bonnet then hide more than they should. Sunglasses on a sunny day help rather than hinder."},"4371":{"text":"As speed rises the angle of vision narrows, because the eyes focus further and further ahead. At 50 km/h you see wide, at 130 km/h practically only a narrow corridor."},"4374":{"text":"On each gear accelerate far enough that after shifting up the engine neither labours nor jerks. Revving to the limiter wastes fuel, and skipping two gears bogs the engine down."},"4375":{"law":"art. 61 ust. 3 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Bicycles may be carried on a roof rack, because there they cover neither the lights nor the number plate. A rear carrier is allowed only if the plate and lights stay visible."},"4472":{"law":"art. 81 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Periodic inspections matter throughout the life of the vehicle, because brakes, suspension and lights wear out regardless of any warranty. A warranty covers repairs, not road safety."},"4495":{"text":"ABS stops the wheels from locking under braking, so the car stays steerable and stable. It does not, however, prevent skidding at any speed and does not help through bends."},"4534":{"text":"On snow everything is done smoothly, with no sudden steering, because grip is minimal. Turning traction control off or accelerating on a climb ends in wheelspin and a skid."},"4562":{"law":"art. 162 Kodeksu karnego","text":"Anyone who could have helped without exposing themselves or others to death or serious harm is liable. The duty is not limited to doctors or to those involved in the crash."},"4563":{"text":"A casualty is pulled out of the vehicle only when life cannot be saved otherwise, for example in cardiac arrest or a fire. Without that need, moving them risks additional spinal injury."},"4578":{"text":"The dispatcher first needs to know where it happened and how many casualties there are and in what condition. That decides how many units and of what kind are sent."},"4579":{"text":"Burning clothing is put out by laying the person down and smothering the flames with a jacket or blanket to cut off the air. A powder extinguisher would further damage the airways and burnt skin."},"4592":{"text":"With no working brake lights the driver behind cannot tell that you are braking, so the car must not be used. Parking sensors and air conditioning have no bearing on road safety."},"4593":{"text":"A red oil pressure lamp means the engine is running without lubrication, so stop and switch it off at once. A dozen more seconds of driving can seize the engine."},"4600":{"text":"112 is the single emergency number: it reaches the ambulance service, the fire brigade and the police at once. It works across Poland and the whole European Union, even from a phone with no SIM card."},"469":{"text":"Red and yellow are lit together, which signals that green is about to come on. You may not move yet, but you can get the car ready to go."},"475":{"law":"sygnalizator S-2, rozporządzenie w sprawie znaków i sygnałów drogowych","text":"Beside the red light a green arrow for a conditional right turn is lit. It permits the turn only after stopping at the signal and giving way to everyone, pedestrians on the crossing included."},"477":{"law":"sygnalizator kierunkowy S-3, rozporządzenie w sprawie znaków i sygnałów drogowych","text":"Your lane is controlled by a directional signal showing a green left arrow. Such a signal permits travel only in the direction of the arrow, that is a left turn, but not a U-turn."},"478":{"law":"sygnalizator kierunkowy S-3, rozporządzenie w sprawie znaków i sygnałów drogowych","text":"The green right arrow is lit in place of the green light, so this is a directional signal. Directional signalling is conflict-free: travelling in the indicated direction you cross no other stream, pedestrians included."},"480":{"text":"Your lane is showing a red signal, and red absolutely forbids passing the signal. You must stop before the signal head or before the stop line."},"486":{"law":"sygnalizator kierunkowy S-3, rozporządzenie w sprawie znaków i sygnałów drogowych","text":"The directional signal shows a green arrow pointing up, so it permits only going straight on. A right turn is prohibited regardless of whether it would obstruct anyone."},"544":{"law":"art. 22 ust. 1 i 4 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The lanes are separated by a broken line, so changing lanes is allowed. You only have to signal with the indicator and give way to any vehicle already in the lane you are moving into."},"589":{"text":"Under the one-way sign there is a plate excluding bicycles, and along the left edge runs a lane with a bicycle symbol. This is contraflow cycling: cyclists legally ride towards you here."},"591":{"text":"The lane on the left is separated by a solid yellow line, temporary marking from roadworks. Yellow marking overrides white, and a solid line must not be crossed."},"627":{"text":"The centre of the road carries a double line: solid on your side, broken on the other. Such a line may be crossed only from the side where it is broken, so you may not cross it."},"6318":{"text":"Alcohol changes the field of vision: it narrows it and weakens peripheral sight and distance judgement. The driver looks straight ahead and does not register a pedestrian stepping in from the side."},"6340":{"text":"An airbag reduces injuries but does not fully protect, and it only works together with a fastened seat belt. It does not protect the bodywork at all, that is what the crumple zones are for."},"6361":{"law":"art. 51 ust. 3 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Main beam must not be used when another vehicle is coming towards you, because it dazzles its driver. Rain or entering a town do not by themselves create that duty."},"6362":{"law":"art. 51 ust. 3 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"You switch to dipped beam whenever you could dazzle the driver ahead, including through their mirrors. Merely seeing a car far ahead does not yet create that duty."},"6378":{"text":"A properly set door mirror shows the area behind the car plus a narrow strip of its own side, which serves as a reference point. Only the side of the car, or only the next lane, is not enough."},"6442":{"text":"Position lights show others where the vehicle is and how wide it is. They do not light the road, and lane changes are signalled with the indicators."},"6443":{"text":"Headlights aimed too high shine into the eyes of oncoming drivers. Their aim has no effect on fuel or bulb consumption."},"6451":{"text":"Headlights aimed too low light only a few metres ahead, so at night you see the road far worse. They have no effect on fuel or bulb consumption."},"6463":{"text":"For a hypothermic person call help, move them somewhere warm, cover them and rewarm slowly. A hot drink and alcohol widen the skin vessels and speed up heat loss from the body core."},"7445":{"law":"art. 60 ust. 2 pkt 4 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Towing children on a sledge behind the car is prohibited. A light trailer is allowed, and so is towing another car inside a built-up area."},"7446":{"law":"art. 19 ust. 3b Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Standing in a tunnel traffic jam you must leave at least 5 metres to the vehicle in front. That gap lets the emergency services through and lets you drive out if a fire breaks out."},"7447":{"law":"art. 45 ust. 2 pkt 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Talking on a hand-held phone is prohibited. The radio and the navigation are allowed, as long as operating them does not take your attention off the road."},"7451":{"law":"art. 61 ust. 8 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A load protruding at the rear is marked with a red flag or plate, and after dark also with a red light and reflector. Red is the warning colour used at the rear in traffic."},"7452":{"text":"The actual total mass of the trailer must not exceed the actual total mass of the car towing it. A heavier trailer starts steering the car instead of being steered."},"7454":{"law":"art. 31 ust. 2 pkt 5 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Towing is prohibited on a motorway, except by a purpose-built recovery vehicle as far as the nearest exit. On an expressway and in a residential zone towing is allowed."},"7457":{"law":"art. 61 ust. 6 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Chains are fitted only on a road covered with snow. On bare tarmac they wreck both the surface and the tyre, and neither the date nor the temperature decides this."},"7461":{"text":"The longest braking distance is on ice, where tyre grip is several times lower than on dry tarmac. A wet road lengthens braking too, but nowhere near as drastically."},"7463":{"text":"ABS lets you keep control under hard braking, because the wheels do not lock and the steering keeps working. It does not always shorten the braking distance: on gravel or snow it can even lengthen it."},"7465":{"law":"art. 46 ust. 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A vehicle left on a slope must be secured against rolling away: parking brake, a gear engaged and the wheels turned towards the kerb. On a steep hill a gear alone is sometimes not enough."},"748":{"law":"art. 24 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"You are on a carriageway with two lanes in your direction, the lanes are separated by a broken line, the signal is green and no overtaking ban applies. You overtake in the left lane, once you have checked it is clear."},"7512":{"law":"art. 31 ust. 1 pkt 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A towed vehicle is marked with a reflective triangle placed at the rear on the left, plus lights on in poor visibility. Hazard lights alone are not a substitute."},"7513":{"law":"art. 78 ust. 4 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"The owner must say to whom the vehicle was entrusted, and the only excuse is that the car was used against their will and knowledge and they could not prevent it. Running a business is no exemption."},"7515":{"law":"art. 60 ust. 1 pkt 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Driving with an obscured number plate is prohibited, because the vehicle cannot be identified. A load covering the plate is no excuse, the load has to be carried differently."},"7516":{"text":"A sticker showing a country other than the one of registration is prohibited, because it misleads about where the vehicle comes from. A plate with the PL symbol changes nothing here."},"7518":{"text":"Faster flashing of the tell-tale is the standard signal that one indicator bulb has burnt out. So you check the bulbs, not the battery, because everything else works normally."},"7519":{"text":"Check the oil level on a cold engine before setting off, or a few minutes after switching off, once the oil has drained into the sump. Measuring right after shutdown or with the engine running gives too low a reading."},"7708":{"text":"On a dry surface you move off in first gear, because it gives the most tractive force. Second gear is only for a very slippery road, when you want to limit wheelspin."},"788":{"law":"art. 24 ust. 6 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A driver who has just been overtaken must not increase speed during the manoeuvre or directly after it. Accelerating now would keep the overtaking car on the opposite lane for longer."},"8320":{"law":"art. 24 ust. 5 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"A rail vehicle is normally overtaken on the right, but on a one-way carriageway it may also be passed on the left. On a one-way road there is no oncoming traffic, so the manoeuvre is safe."},"891":{"text":"Sign A-1 warns of one dangerous bend to the right. Were there more bends, the sign here would be A-3 with two curves, not one."},"892":{"text":"Sign A-2 warns of a single dangerous bend to the left, not of several. A series of bends is announced by the sign with two curves, A-3 or A-4."},"893":{"text":"Under the bends sign hangs a plate with the figure 3, which states how many bends lie ahead. Since there are three, the answer about two bends is wrong."},"894":{"text":"Sign A-4 warns of two dangerous bends, the first of them to the left. With no number plate, the sign with two curves means exactly two bends."},"898":{"law":"art. 25 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Sign A-5 warns of a crossroads of equal roads, where no signs determine priority. The right-hand rule applies: you give way to a vehicle coming from your right."},"9012":{"text":"The driver influences visual acuity themselves: through concentration, how they feel and their state of health, including fatigue and eyesight. Weather, road surface and time of day are external conditions they cannot change."},"9035":{"text":"The higher the speed, the narrower the field of vision: at 40 km/h it spans about a hundred degrees, at 130 km/h only a few dozen. That is why on a fast road it is easy to miss what happens at the side."},"9058":{"law":"art. 60 ust. 2 pkt 2 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Excessive exhaust emissions and excessive noise are prohibited everywhere, not only in town or in a residential zone. The rule protects the environment and people across the whole road network."},"9065":{"text":"ASR acts when drive is fed to the wheels, so it helps during sudden acceleration on a wet surface. Going downhill the wheels are not driven and the system has nothing to correct."},"9067":{"text":"ASR is most useful when pulling away hard on a slippery surface, because that is when the driven wheels spin. Going downhill or climbing steadily there is no wheelspin for it to limit."},"9068":{"text":"ESP steps in where the car stops following the intended line, that is in a sharp bend. At a steady speed or on a straight there is nothing to stabilise."},"9070":{"text":"Several bends one after another are the classic case where the body starts to sway and ESP corrects the line. Holding a steady speed is the job of cruise control, not ESP."},"916":{"text":"With time at the wheel attention falls rather than rises: fatigue and monotony reduce your ability to notice signs and signals. That is why on a long trip you break roughly every two hours."},"974":{"text":"The variable message board is showing a warning sign for a slippery road together with a call to drive carefully. A warning sign always announces a place where danger exists or may arise."},"975":{"law":"art. 3 ust. 1 Prawa o ruchu drogowym","text":"Above every lane the A-30 sign is displayed, a warning of other danger. Every warning sign imposes a duty of particular caution up to the place it refers to."},"978":{"text":"The sign warns of a one-way road joining: the arrow in the symbol shows that vehicles can only enter your road from there. That road is subordinate, but drivers coming off it still manage to force their way in."},"980":{"text":"Under the give-way sign hangs a T-6 plate, which draws the actual course of the priority road through this junction. The thick line is the main road, the thin one is your approach."},"985":{"text":"Sign A-9 with the gate symbol warns of a level crossing with barriers or half-barriers. A crossing without barriers is announced by sign A-10 with the locomotive symbol."},"986":{"text":"The sign shows a locomotive, so it is A-10: a level crossing without barriers. Nothing there will close the road in front of a train, so checking is entirely on you."},"987":{"text":"The locomotive symbol means sign A-10, a crossing with neither barriers nor half-barriers. Barriers would be announced by sign A-9 with the gate symbol."},"988":{"text":"Sign A-11 warns of an uneven road, that is transverse unevenness of the surface: ruts, humps, potholes. Slow down, because on unevenness the car loses grip and stability."},"990":{"text":"Under the uneven road sign hangs a T-2 plate with the length of the section: the unevenness runs for 1.2 km. A length plate always says how far the hazard extends, not how far away it starts."},"991":{"text":"The sign shows two bumps, so it is A-11: uneven road, damaged surface. A speed hump is announced by A-11a, which carries a single distinct hump."},"992":{"text":"Sign A-11a with a single pronounced hump marks a speed bump, laid there to force slower driving. The plate says the bump is 25 metres beyond the sign."},"994":{"text":"The T-1 plate gives the distance from the sign to the hazard, here 25 metres to the speed bump. The length of the hazardous section itself is given by a different plate, T-2."},"996":{"text":"Sign A-12a warns of the carriageway narrowing on both sides. A narrower road leaves less room for passing oncoming traffic, so slow down and give way if needed."},"997":{"text":"Signs A-6b and A-6c differ only in the side the subordinate road joins from, and the pictogram shows which. Here the junction is not on the right, so the answer is no."}};
